##  TypeScript End-User API for 3D Camera Animation (Prioritizing Helpfulness & Verbosity)

This API aims to be intuitive, robust, and  developer-friendly for seamlessly integrating 3D camera animations into TypeScript applications. We'll leverage common animation principles and offer flexibility while maintaining clarity.

**Core Concepts & Structure:**

1. **`CameraController` Class:**  The central hub managing camera behavior. Instances represent individual cameras within your scene.

   ```typescript
   class CameraController {
       constructor(scene: THREE.Scene, initialPosition: THREE.Vector3, target?: THREE.Object3D) {
           this.scene = scene;
           this.camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(/* ... setup with initialPosition, field of view, etc. */);
           this.target = target || new THREE.Object3D(); // Default target if none provided
           this.animationStack = []; // Internal for managing queued animations
       }

       // Animation Methods (detailed below)
       animateTo(targetPos: THREE.Vector3, duration: number, easing?: EasingFunction): this {
           // ... internally queues an animation (see animation implementation)
           return this;
       }

       smoothTrack(targetObject: THREE.Object3D, duration: number, easing?: EasingFunction): this {
           // ...  queues continuous tracking animation, adjusts based on target movement
           return this;
       }

       // ... Other methods like pan, dolly, rotate, presets, etc.

       start(): void {  this.animateLoop(); } // Initiate animation playback loop
       stop(): void { /* Clear internal animation queue and pause */ }
   }
   ```

2. **Animation Types & Fluent API:**

   * **`animateTo(targetPos, duration, easing)`:**  Directly moves the camera to a specified position over a given duration using a chosen easing function.
   * **`smoothTrack(targetObject, duration, easing)`:**  Continuously follows a moving object, dynamically adjusting camera position for a smooth chase effect. Ideal for character or entity tracking.
   * **`pan(direction: 'left'/'right'/'up'/'down', distance: number, duration)`:**  Controlled horizontal or vertical camera shifts.
   * **`dolly(distance: number, duration, easing)`:**  Zooms the camera towards or

```dart
import 'dart:collection';

class Transaction {
  final String coinName;
  final DateTime datetime;
  final double profitLoss;

  Transaction({required this.coinName, required this.datetime, required this.profitLoss});
}

Future<Map<String, dynamic>> analyzeProfitsLosses(List<Transaction> transactions) async {
  // Group transactions by coin name for aggregation
  final groupedTransactions = transactions.groupBy((transaction) => transaction.coinName);

  // Calculate average profit/loss per coin
  final avgProfits = <String, double>{};
  final avgLosses = <String, double>{};
  for (var (coin, transactionsGroup) in groupedTransactions.entries) {
    double totalProfit = 0;
    double totalLoss = 0;
    for (var transaction in transactionsGroup) {
      totalProfit += transaction.profitLoss > 0 ? transaction.profitLoss : 0;
      totalLoss += transaction.profitLoss < 0 ? -transaction.profitLoss : 0;
    }
    avgProfits[coin] = totalProfit / transactionsGroup.length;
    avgLosses[coin] = totalLoss / transactionsGroup.length;
  }

  // Extract top 3 with highest average profit and loss
  final topProfits = avgProfits.entries.toList()
    ..sort((a, b) => b.value.compareTo(a.value)) // Descending order
    ..take(3)
    ..map((entry) => {'coin': entry.key, 'averageProfit': entry.value})
    .toList();

  final topLosses = avgLosses.entries.toList()
    ..sort((a, b) => b.value.compareTo(a.value)) // Descending order
    ..take(3)
    ..map((entry) => {'coin': entry.key, 'averageLoss': entry.value})
    .toList();

  return {'topProfits': topProfits, 'topLosses': topLosses};
}
```

**Explanation and Weighted Rating Optimization:**

